\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I sing the almighty power of God, 
\par That made the mountains rise, 
\par That spread the flowing seas abroad,
\par And built the lofty skies.
\par   \tab 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I sing the wisdom that ordained
\par The sun to rule the day;
\par The moon shines full at His command, 
\par And all the stars obey.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I sing the goodness of the Lord, 
\par That filled the earth with food;
\par He formed the creatures with His word,
\par And then pronounced them good.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, how Thy wonders are displayed
\par Where'er I turn mine eye,
\par If I survey the ground I tread, 
\par Or gaze upon the sky; 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. There's not a plant or flower below
\par But makes Thy glories known,
\par And clouds arise and tempests blow 
\par By order from Thy throne. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. God's hand is my perpetual guard, 
\par He guides me with His eye;   \tab 
\par Why should I then forget the Lord? 
\par Whose love is ever nigh?
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

